        "evidence": "At native scale the long open herringbone coat and its hanging lower panels are clear, but the required side-panel-to-torso air gap is not independently visible. The flank is covered by coat fabric and the working forearm; the open front exposing the knit and lower gaps beside the thighs do not establish a gap beside the torso. Partial/hidden evidence remains failure, not a conclusion that the body or fit is defective.",
